# Copy to openspec/config.yml after running `openspec init`.
# This is what makes the generated artifacts speak your project's language instead
# of generic software-engineering prose.

context: |
  Monorepo with two deployable services:
  - business-backend/ : Ruby on Rails 8. Frontend + business backend. Users, sessions,
    persistence, business rules. The only publicly exposed service. Tests are Minitest
    under test/, run with `bin/rails test`.
  - ai-service/ : Python 3.11 + FastAPI. LLM calls, CAG/RAG pipeline, agent and graph
    orchestration. Private network only, authenticated with the X-Service-Token
    middleware plus per-router X-API-Key. Never exposed publicly. Tests run with
    `uv run pytest`.

  Datastores: two PostgreSQL instances — `postgres` (relational, owned by Rails) and
  `vector-db` (pgvector, owned by the AI service). Neither reads the other's data.
  Redis Stack backs the semantic cache and the runtime config.

  AI service layers, outermost import first: foundation/ -> domain/ -> generation/
  (cag, rag, agentic, conversation) -> ingestion/ -> api/. A generation sibling never
  imports another generation sibling; they compose only inside a conductor in domain/.
  Routers are transport only.

  Business backend: contexts (estimation, conversation, rag, agents) over the
  EstimatorAi foundation in app/services/estimator_ai/, which is the ONLY layer that
  speaks HTTP to the AI service. Contract POROs mirror the Pydantic schemas 1:1.

  Domain: software effort estimation. A transcript or a task description goes in; a
  structured estimate comes out, grounded in a corpus of historical budgets and tasks
  retrieved from the vector database, with its supporting sources and a confidence.

  Two URL prefixes coexist on purpose: /api/v1/* (Session 4 estimate, sessions,
  ingestion, config) and /v1/* (Session 9+ RAG, graph and supervisor routes). The
  routes the business backend consumes are pinned in
  docs/contract/business-backend-consumed-routes.json and verified in CI by
  ai-service/scripts/check_contract.py.

  Never write "backend" unqualified. Use "ai-service" or "business-backend".

  All code, comments, logs, tests, commit messages and API schemas are written in
  English. The prose documentation under docs/ is written in Spanish, except the five
  standards documents below, which the agent reads and which stay in English.

  Project standards (single source of truth). Read and apply these before creating
  any artifact or writing any code:
  - docs/base-standards.md — core principles, decision closure, definition of done
  - docs/doc-architecture.md — layers, ownership boundaries, the contract between layers
  - docs/doc-verification-guide.md — which verification path proves which change
  - docs/ai-service-standards.md — FastAPI layering, schemas, typed errors, guardrails
  - docs/business-backend-standards.md — Rails client boundary, degradation, persistence

  Use ai-specs/skills/ for workflow guidance. Use templates/ for artifact shapes.

rules:
  _global:
    - Before creating any artifact, read docs/base-standards.md
    - >-
      Forbidden in any artifact when it affects behaviour: "if needed", "if applicable",
      "when available", "if present", "optional depending on", "or", "prefer", "may be".
      If you cannot remove the word, ask a blocking question instead.
    - Every externally visible field must declare presence, source of truth,
      missing-data behaviour and transformation rule.
    - Every requirement needs at least one failure scenario.
    - Cite real files from this repository. Never invent a path, a route or a symbol;
      read the code first and name what you actually found.

  proposal:
    - State explicitly which of the two services owns each new responsibility.
    - State explicitly whether the contract changes, whether
      docs/contract/business-backend-consumed-routes.json must be updated, and whether
      the change is backward compatible.
    - For the AI service, name the layer (foundation / domain / generation / api) and
      justify it against docs/doc-architecture.md.

  tasks:
    - Task 0 is always "create the feature branch".
    - Verification tasks are executed by the agent, never delegated to the user.
    - Use `uv run pytest` for the AI service and `bin/rails test` for the business
      backend. There is no tests/unit, tests/integration or tests/e2e split, and the
      business backend does not use RSpec.
    - A task may only be marked [x] once its verification evidence exists.
    - End the file with the Execution Report template.
